<section style="padding:96px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>An expired oil tank in Newfoundland turns from paperwork into a real problem the minute the fuel truck pulls up. The driver reads the HOST tag, sees a date that's already passed or spots rust, a leaning stand or a weeping fitting, and under NLR 60/03 they can't fill you and have to report what they found. In a St. John's January, that's a no-heat emergency by suppertime.</p><p>Harbour Tank Co answers expired-tag and leaking-tank calls 24/7 across St. John's and the Avalon Peninsula. We'll tell you what to shut off and what to leave alone on the phone, then get a crew out to swap the tank or deal with the leak. A new 200-gallon steel tank is $3,200 installed with the old one hauled away, and every job starts with a free written estimate. Call (709) 800-3117, or keep reading for what to do while you wait.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Answered any hour</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A refused delivery at 4 pm on a Friday or an oil smell at midnight gets a real person at (709) 800-3117. We'll tell you what to shut off, what to leave alone, and when we can be there.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Refused delivery, sorted</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Under section 13 of NLR 60/03 the driver can't fill an expired or deficient tank, full stop. We swap the tank, the installer's licensed inspector tags and registers it, and you rebook your delivery with a current date on the tag.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Leak triage on the phone</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Tell us what you see and smell and we'll help you work out whether it's a drip at a fitting or a tank shell letting go. That decides whether you need us tonight or first thing tomorrow.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">The 10-day clock, handled</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">After a leak, section 18(5) gives you 10 days to empty, dismantle and dispose of the tank. We book the removal inside that window so the deadline isn't sitting on your shoulders.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Storm damage checks</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">After a big Avalon blow we'll look at the legs, the pad, the fill and vent pipes and the line to the furnace, then tell you plainly whether the tank is safe to run until it's replaced.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Straight prices, in writing</h3>
